From: johnpatrickwarren-oss <john.patrick.warren@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add chaos_experiment to event_class closed-set (DS-Anvil Addition #29)

DeploySignal's Anvil capability (Addition #29 / PRD-29 / Q29) extends
the DS engine with a chaos-engineering verdict layer. The DS-Anvil
buyer bundle (DS + Tessera + chaos-adapter family) composes by reusing
Tessera's existing ds-integration HTTP contract: when an Anvil chaos
run starts, DeploySignal emits a `chaos_experiment` event so Tessera's
freeze-hook activates over the experiment's declared fault window —
same semantic as the other 5 event classes.

This patch is backward-additive: existing 5-value behavior unchanged;
6th value added to the closed-set. The mapEventClassToKind switch and
the AC-R66-17 parity test follow the established symmetry between
event-feed.ts and event-contract.ts.

Cross-repo reference: https://github.com/johnpatrickwarren-oss/deploysignal/pull/19
                      coordination/PRD-29-anvil.md § Dependencies
                      coordination/Q29-ANVIL-CHAOS-VERDICT-SPEC.md § Anti-scope

To apply:
    cd /path/to/tessera
    git checkout -b feat/chaos-experiment-event-class
    git apply path/to/TESSERA-CHAOS-EXPERIMENT-EVENT-CLASS.patch
    pnpm install && pnpm test    # verify AC-R66-7 + AC-R66-17 pass
    git add -A && git commit
    gh pr create

